It'd be more interesting if it was avg damage vs monsters that are
actually a threat by the time you've got them enchanted up.  That's
pretty much the Sanctum/Air/Astral.  And maybe how fast I can kill
Orcus (to save some charges).

>  - 10% demon
>  - 10% dragon
>  -  5% giant
>  -  3% troll
>  -  2% ogre
>  -  1% lycanthrope
>  -  1% orc

The latter 3 are all pointless by the time you enchant things up.
They're basically meat-shields that keep the tougher stuff at bay when
you're swarmed, and not a threat when you're not.  Giants, dragons,
most demons, and non-Olag Hai trolls aren't too far off of the same
category.

Damage output is only useful inasmuch as it helps you survive, so it's
worth biasing toward weapons that are more effective in the most
dangerous parts of the game even if they have lower damage output
overall.  If you're alone in a hallway, taking an extra hit or two to
take out most monsters isn't a big hit on your survivability.  When
you're swamped in Air, taking out that Archon a turn earlier could be
very important.


